1
00:00:00,767 --> 00:00:03,935
This is Cedar: an open
source assistant that runs

2
00:00:03,935 --> 00:00:07,102
on your own computer, and
does real work for you.

3
00:00:09,723 --> 00:00:14,664
The first time you open it, Cedar asks
which language you'd like to work in.

4
00:00:14,664 --> 00:00:18,435
After that it needs just one
thing: a model to think with.

5
00:00:21,943 --> 00:00:24,424
Cedar isn't tied to one AI company.

6
00:00:24,424 --> 00:00:28,820
Under Settings, Models, you choose
where the model comes from.

7
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:31,443
The Cedar app for Mac and Windows can

8
00:00:31,443 --> 00:00:34,775
download one and run it
for you with llama.cpp.

9
00:00:34,775 --> 00:00:38,037
You can use a hosted
provider with an API key.

10
00:00:38,037 --> 00:00:42,078
Or you can point Cedar at a
model server you already run.

11
00:00:42,078 --> 00:00:44,488
Here, that's vLLM on this machine.

12
00:00:44,488 --> 00:00:47,395
Cedar lists the models the server offers.

13
00:00:47,395 --> 00:00:51,861
Pick one, and it fills in the
reasoning levels the model takes,

14
00:00:51,861 --> 00:00:54,059
and whether it can read images.

15
00:00:54,059 --> 00:00:57,675
Then it checks the address
once more, and saves it.

16
00:01:04,659 --> 00:01:05,589
Now for a task.

17
00:01:05,589 --> 00:01:08,130
I'll attach a year of household spending,

18
00:01:08,130 --> 00:01:11,043
and ask Cedar to work out
where the money goes,

19
00:01:11,043 --> 00:01:14,948
chart it, and write a one-page
summary with three ways to save.

20
00:01:21,026 --> 00:01:22,722
Cedar doesn't just start.

21
00:01:22,722 --> 00:01:25,912
For a bigger task, it
shows you its plan first.

22
00:01:25,912 --> 00:01:29,372
You can reword a step,
remove one, or add your own.

23
00:01:29,372 --> 00:01:31,951
When it looks right, tell it to start.

24
00:01:36,893 --> 00:01:40,719
The work happens in a sealed
box: a container of its own,

25
00:01:40,719 --> 00:01:44,947
with the network off, that can't
see the rest of your computer.

26
00:01:44,947 --> 00:01:49,645
Cedar runs the numbers in Python,
draws the chart, and writes the PDF.

27
00:01:49,645 --> 00:01:52,062
Each step stays in the conversation,

28
00:01:52,062 --> 00:01:55,015
so you can open it and
see exactly what ran.

29
00:02:01,764 --> 00:02:06,399
The chart is interactive: point at
a month to read every category.

30
00:02:06,399 --> 00:02:09,138
The finished summary sits on the right,

31
00:02:09,138 --> 00:02:12,369
with the three suggestions,
ready to download.

32
00:02:12,369 --> 00:02:15,529
And the short version
is in the conversation.

33
00:02:26,879 --> 00:02:29,487
Some things Cedar won't do on its own.

34
00:02:29,487 --> 00:02:33,125
Ask it to delete a file, and
it stops and asks first.

35
00:02:33,125 --> 00:02:36,969
Downloads, installs and sending
email work the same way.

36
00:02:36,969 --> 00:02:39,578
Nothing risky happens without your OK.

37
00:02:42,366 --> 00:02:45,239
Cedar also remembers what you ask it to.

38
00:02:45,239 --> 00:02:49,909
Under Settings, Memory, you see
everything it has kept about you.

39
00:02:49,909 --> 00:02:52,926
Pin it, archive it, or remove it for good.

40
00:02:52,926 --> 00:02:55,368
It stays on your own Cedar server.

41
00:03:05,243 --> 00:03:07,267
Every ability has a switch.

42
00:03:07,267 --> 00:03:11,240
Reading web pages, weather,
maps, directions, stocks.

43
00:03:11,240 --> 00:03:13,414
Turn on what Cedar may reach.

44
00:03:13,414 --> 00:03:15,363
Everything else stays off.

45
00:03:18,572 --> 00:03:22,655
And when a conversation did its
job, turn it into an agent.

46
00:03:22,655 --> 00:03:25,838
Cedar writes the prompt
from the conversation.

47
00:03:25,838 --> 00:03:28,468
You choose what starts it: a schedule,

48
00:03:28,468 --> 00:03:31,997
a change it watches for,
new mail, a file arriving.

49
00:03:31,997 --> 00:03:34,073
This one will run every month.

50
00:03:41,289 --> 00:03:43,466
Cedar is free and open source.

51
00:03:43,466 --> 00:03:48,402
It runs on Mac, Windows and Linux,
with apps for iPhone and Android.

52
00:03:48,402 --> 00:03:49,781
Your own assistant.

53
00:03:49,781 --> 00:03:51,886
Runs at home, answers to you.
